\label{lem:ideal-output}
The evaluations of the $r$ output expressions in the symbolic
simulation form a basis of $V$ with probability at most $\rho_r$.

\label{thm:quantitative}
Let an algorithm perform at most $q$ group additions and output
$r$ labels. If $M=3q+r+1\leq n=2^r$, then
\begin{equation}\label{eq:success}
    \mathop{\rm Pr}_{G\sim\mathcal D_r}
    [\text{the output is a basis}]
    \leq
    \rho_r+\frac{\binom{3q+r+1}{2}}{n}.
\end{equation}
For a randomized algorithm, the probability also includes its
internal random choices, and the bound of $q$ additions must
hold on every execution.
